      "writtenOn": "2026-11-04T22:21:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The approach im currently going with is treating non-present properties as \"ok\",  and allowing the power on.\n\nAre there any properties among the ones we have that can always be assumed to exist on a chassis (i.e present?) Or can this assumption not be made?\n\nIn the case where a chassis implements none of the properties we\u0027ve established - should we allow it to power on?",
      "parentUuid": "67fe2a42_d3194af4",
      "revId": "d34beae6bd2d5a4c9a3609286e58d2a836b8cc25",
