      "writtenOn": "2026-11-05T16:02:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What we\u0027ve done in some of the phosphor-power apps is specify which properties are being checked for a particular system type in a JSON config file.\n\nThen in the C++ implementation, it does the following:\n- If a property is not being checked, just immediately return that it is fine (e.g. chassis is present, available, etc.)\n- If a property is being checked, get the value from D-Bus. If we can\u0027t get the value, that is an error situation (app that publishes it not working, systemd boot order issue, etc.)\n\nNot sure if that would help here.\n\nWithout information from the JSON file, it is tricky to know how to handle a \u0027missing\u0027 property on D-Bus. For example, if Available is not being used, then it probably won\u0027t be on D-Bus. But if it is being used, and it isn\u0027t on D-Bus, then we don\u0027t know whether a chassis can be powered on.\n\nWould be interested in Andrew\u0027s opinion though since he knows this repo and I don\u0027t.",
      "parentUuid": "a45902cd_4b49ee9d",
